  66:     Complete same-color marker segments inside a regular lattice of framed tiles.
  67: 
  68:     Input structure
  69:     - The grid is partitioned by separator rows and columns into 4x4 framed tiles.
  70:     - All tile borders have one frame color, and each 2x2 tile interior has a dominant fill color.
  71:     - Other interior colors are endpoint markers, with their exact 2x2 subcell position preserved.
  72: 
  73:     Rule
  74:     - Group endpoint markers by marker color and by their relative interior subcell.
  75:     - When two or more endpoints in a group share a tile row, fill every intervening tile at that same subcell with the marker color.
  76:     - When two or more endpoints in a group share a tile column, fill every intervening tile at that same subcell with the marker color.
  77: 
  78:     Key insight
  79:     - The colored endpoints are not connected in pixel space; they are connected on the coarser tile lattice, and the chosen interior subcell identifies which lane to paint.
